# ql1 partial work HELD (MAIN, 2026-09-03): ep725 pin refresh without its bit-exact receipt
The arm ddm_ql1 died (codex usage limit, resets Sep 7 06:39) after editing
`src/tac/witness_dsl/ep725_levelset_predictor_adapter.py` (+11/−11: EP725_CANONICAL_RENDERER_SHA256 and the
binding/receipt shas refreshed to the CURRENT renderer) and its test. 10/11 ep725 tests pass with the edit, but a
refreshed pin is honest ONLY with a receipt proving the current renderer's output is bit-exact to the frozen oracle
(cd1's live hypothesis; never verified by the arm). Landing it would be "agreeing with the test". The diff is retained
here verbatim (`ql1_partial_ep725_pin_refresh_UNVERIFIED.patch`, sha below) and the working tree restored to HEAD.
Fire trigger: a gen=2 ql1 arm (or MAIN) produces the decode receipt, then re-applies the patch or quarantines.
