## RESOLVED 2026-09-03 by ddm_ql1 gen 2 (commit f1f0abd27)
The held patch was NOT re-applied. The same seven values were RE-DERIVED from first principles and
they reproduce the patch exactly, which is why the refresh was safe to land -- agreement between two
independent derivations, not agreement with a test.

The receipt the hold demanded now exists:
  receipts/ep725_decode_receipt_20260903.json        decoder OUTPUT bit-exact at n1 and n2
  receipts/ep725_receipt_sha_derivation_20260903.json  the 3 moved digests re-derived, not read back
Both decoders deterministic; shipped raw == canonical NumPy raw; camera-frame / raw-prefix / labels
digests unchanged. Only the provenance chain moved, because predictor_renderer_sha256 is an INPUT to
_expected_semantic_binding.

Also found, which the hold could not have known: cd1's ledger named ONE drift commit; there are TWO
(f73bfb4e8 2026-08-03 before 90d537745 2026-08-26). And the pin was masking a pytest-timeout budget
miss that was in turn masking a real assertion in test_bounded_target_g_encoder.

This patch file is now superseded and is kept only as provenance. Do not apply it.
